           {
            "answer": "Three reasons. Quality: US production sites operate under FDA oversight with consistent enforcement. Supply chain: shorter lead times, lower freight costs and less disruption risk. Marketing: Made in the USA resonates with a large share of supplement buyers and is verifiable in your claims.",
            "question": "Why does US manufacturing matter for supplement brands?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "Yes. Praxera products are made in a Vermont facility that has been continuously FDA-registered since registration was first required, and that is GMP-certified to NSF 455-2, the most rigorous supplement-specific GMP standard.",
            "question": "Is the facility FDA-registered?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "Per unit it can be, depending on the formulation. Total landed cost - after shipping, duties, quality risk and turnaround time - often makes US manufacturing cost-competitive or better. Most brands that price it out side by side choose US manufacturing for reasons beyond unit cost.",
            "question": "Is US manufacturing more expensive than overseas?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "Yes. Tours can be arranged for prospective and active clients. Ask your Praxera contact, or request one using the form on this page.",
            "question": "Can I tour the site where my products are made?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "Most stock formulations have minimums in the low hundreds of bottles per SKU. The exact number depends on the formulation and we confirm it during your consultation.",
            "question": "What's the minimum order size to work with you?"
           }
